<title>GREECE: GREEK NATL MORTGAGE, BEAR STEARNS TO SIGN DEAL.</title>
<headline>GREEK NATL MORTGAGE, BEAR STEARNS TO SIGN DEAL.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's state National Mortgage Bank and Bear Stearns will sign an agreement for the securitisation of National Mortgage Bank mortgages April 22, its president Vassilis Rapanos told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;We will sign an agreement with Bear Stearns for the securitisation of our mortgages next Tuesday,&quot; said Rapanos.</p>
<p>The agreement will call for a feasibility study to be completed within the next six-to-nine months, he said.</p>
<p>A second phase, expected to last up to three years, will ensue where the securitisation of mortgages will actually take place, he added. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
